      "description": "Not sure which knot you need? Knot IQ helps you choose the right one, then shows you how to tie it in true interactive 3D.\n\nBuilt by The Bear Essentials, Knot IQ is a practical knot-tying guide with 300+ knots for fishing, camping, climbing, boating, bushcraft, rescue, arborist work, scouting, and everyday rope work. Download the enhanced 3D knots you need and keep learning offline.\n\nCHOOSE WITH KNOTFINDER\n\nStart with the job, not the knot’s name. Answer a few quick questions about what you are doing. KnotFINDER narrows the choices, explains why each recommendation fits, and helps you compare your options.\n\nCONTROL EVERY STEP IN TRUE 3D\n\nRotate the knot freely, zoom in, scrub through every step, reverse the sequence, pause, and change the playback speed. Adjust the rope colours for better visibility or switch to left-handed mode.\n\nLEARN WHERE AND WHY A KNOT WORKS\n\nGo beyond memorizing an animation. Review practical uses, strengths, trade-offs, and related knots. Interactive scenes show where knots belong in real situations: tap a task to see what to tie and where.\n\n300+ KNOTS, ORGANIZED YOUR WAY\n\nSearch by name, browse by activity or knot type, filter your library, save favourites, and build custom lists. Use the Downloaded filter to find the 3D knots you have saved for offline learning.\n\nExplore fishing and fly-fishing knots; camping and bushcraft knots; climbing, rescue, and firefighting knots; boating, sailing, and marine knots; arborist, hoisting, and rigging knots; scouting knots and lashings; plus necktie knots, shoelaces, household, utility, decorative, and specialty ropework.\n\nLearn essentials such as the Bowline, Clove Hitch, Figure Eight, Sheet Bend, Taut-Line Hitch, Trucker’s Hitch, Prusik, and Munter Hitch—plus hundreds of specialized bends, bindings, friction hitches, lashings, loops, splices, stopper knots, and quick-release knots.\n\nKEY FEATURES\n\n• 300+ knots and growing\n• True interactive 3D knot models\n• Rotate, zoom, scrub, reverse, pause, and change speed\n• Guided KnotFINDER recommendations with explanations\n• Offline access to downloaded 3D knot resources\n• Interactive scenes and practical use guidance\n• Rope-colour controls and left-handed mode\n• Favourites, custom lists, search, filters, and related knots\n• Expert guides and video tutorials from The Bear Essentials\n• One-time purchase with no ads or subscriptions\n• No data collected\n• Apple Family Sharing\n\nMade for beginners and experienced knot tyers alike. Learn. Craft. Explore.\n\nSafety note: Knot IQ is an educational reference. For climbing, rescue, arborist, marine, and other safety-critical uses, follow qualified instruction, inspect your equipment, and use the procedures required for your activity.",
